The city shall have authority after reasonable notice and hearing, to terminate and cancel any franchise granted pursuant to this chapter, and declare a forfeiture of the same, in the event that a company:
(1) Violates any provision of this chapter, as it may be amended from time to time or any rule, order, or determination of the commission made pursuant to this chapter except where such violation is committed without fault, or through excusable neglect;
(2) Becomes insolvent or unable or unwilling to pay its debts or is adjudged bankrupt;
(3) Attempts to evade any of the provisions of this chapter or the franchise or practices any fraud or deceit upon the city;
(4) Fails to secure a certificate of compliance from the FCC or any other necessary license or permit within four months of the acceptance of a franchise;
(5) Fails to exhibit substantial progress toward the completion of the construction of the system for a period of three consecutive calendar months; or
(6) Fails to pay to the city the franchise fee provided hereinabove after written notice that a payment is overdue.
(Ord. No. 810, § 21, 8-17-1984)

